// A file-scope declaration the C89 side cannot carry.
//
// This is the case that was missing. SToC counted this refusal and then
// dropped the marker on the way out of the globals holder, so the run
// announced "1 construct has no expression in the target language, and
// each is marked where it stands in the output" over a C file with no
// marker in it at all. A reader told to find one found none, and what
// was left was a program missing a declaration with nothing to say
// where it had been.
//
// The same fault had been found twice on the C-to-Shalimar side and
// fixed there both times; nothing on this side could see it, because
// every counted-equals-shown check in this suite was made of C input.
//
// Shalimar sizes an array at run time, so 'int grid[size]' is ordinary
// here and shc compiles and runs it. C89 sizes arrays when it compiles,
// so there is nowhere for that to go - which makes this a refusal that
// is genuinely about the mapping rather than about the front end.
int size : 3
int grid[size]

fun <> = main() {
  grid[0] : 7
  ? grid[0]
  return
}
